{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationExtensive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationExtensive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.jetBinding_lt_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.jetBinding_lt_succ","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationExtensive.lean#L63-L73","doc":"**Strictly extensive.** A body-order with strictly positive contribution strictly\nincreases the binding. Combined with the (conjectural) super-exponential growth of\n`a_D^(n) = lw(n−1)`, this is the mechanism by which the na-Stokes period supplies the\nextensive `A`-growth of nuclear binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.jetBinding_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.jetBinding_mono","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationExtensive.lean#L50-L61","doc":"**Extensive (monotone).** The jet-filtration binding is monotone non-decreasing in\nthe body-order cutoff `A`: adding nucleon body-orders can only increase binding.\n(The intensive rotation-phase `θ_λ` route lacked this.) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:jet-filtration-binding-extensive","label":"prop:jet-filtration-binding-extensive","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-filtration-binding-extensive.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.jetBinding_term_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.jetBinding_term_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationExtensive.lean#L43-L48","doc":"Each body-order term is non-negative when the electron scale, the SW period, and\nthe residue weight are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.jetBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.jetBinding","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationExtensive.lean#L38-L41","doc":"The body-order (jet-filtration) binding\n`B(A) = Σ_{n=2}^{A} m_e · a_D(n) · w(n)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}